# Whirlpools: keep squaring a number and taking the remainder mod 31.
# Every start falls into a loop sooner or later. `orbit` says how long the
# lead-in (the tail) is and how long the loop is.
: step dup * 31 % ;
use orbits
2 1 [ drop
  dup . ." falls into a loop of length " dup orbit . ." after a tail of " . 10 emit
  1 + dup 13 < ] drop drop
